{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E2JQV8BWDYW84P0MAZC0",
  "name": "web: path traversal — transcript_ref allows arbitrary local file read",
  "slug": "web-path-traversal-transcript-ref-allows-arbitrary-local-fil",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "transcript_ref is an unconstrained string joined onto slopRoot with no containment check, so a tampered/merged session file with ../ segments turns the read-only viewer into an arbitrary-file-read primitive on the host.",
    "details_md": "openTranscript does join(this.slopRoot, transcriptRef) and serves the file. transcript_ref is z.string().nullable() with no path constraint. A .slop/db is a git-mergeable, collaborator-editable store, so a malicious/buggy session file is a realistic input. Reproduced live reading a file two directories above .slop/.",
    "acceptance": [
      "transcript_ref is validated (reject leading /, .., and anything not normalizing under .slop root) at the schema and/or at openTranscript",
      "openTranscript re-checks the resolved absolute path is a prefix of the resolved slop root before opening",
      "A test asserts a session whose transcript_ref escapes the root yields null/404, not file contents"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/web/fixture-data-source.ts:177-186 openTranscript join(slopRoot, transcriptRef)",
      "src/core/entities/session.ts:67 transcript_ref: z.string().nullable()"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
